  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "For U1 (configurable Sqoop metastore), use Spring's DataSource abstraction to support pluggable metastore database implementations, avoiding hardcoded default metastore configuration",
    "For U3 (metrics REST API), extend the existing Spring MVC metrics endpoint structure to add the /all endpoints, reusing the existing metrics collection service to avoid duplicate logic",
    "For U4 (Boot-based ModuleRunner), leverage Spring Boot's CommandLineRunner and auto-configuration abstractions to implement the ModuleRunner, while maintaining backward compatibility with existing xd-container deployments",
    "For U6 (jdbcgpfdist batch job), reuse the existing gpfdist sink module's writer logic, adapt it to Spring Batch's chunk-oriented processing model to align with Spring XD's batch job standards",
    "For U7 (test infrastructure decoupling), use Spring's @Profile annotation and separate test configuration classes to isolate mock beans from real repository beans in the test context",
    "For U8 (reactor module move to core), refactor the existing reactor module code to use core Spring XD module APIs, eliminating the dependency on the spring-xd-modules repository for reactor functionality",
    "All new code follows Spring's existing coding and documentation conventions, and uses JUnit 5 and Mockito for testing",
    "All changes maintain backward compatibility with existing Spring XD 6.0+ deployments, with no breaking public API changes"
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "All required third-party dependencies (Sqoop, Greenplum/GPDB, HAWQ, Project Reactor) are already managed in the project's dependency management system, with no unresolved version conflicts",
    "The referenced StackOverflow thread for U1 and Socialcast post for U5 provide sufficient context for required configuration changes, with no need for additional external research",
    "The existing gpfdist sink code referenced in U6 is well-documented and can be adapted to the batch model without major architectural rework",
    "Existing Spring XD test infrastructure is extensible to support the decoupled mock/real repository setup required for U7",
    "The target runtime for all changes is Spring Framework 6.0+ and Java 17+, as specified in the provided documentation",
    "No new security vulnerabilities are introduced by the configuration changes for U1 and U5, and existing security standards are followed"
  ],
